    material: true,
    summary: 'Topic pages use the new learning path layout and no longer have their own search box, so no page on the site writes what you type into its address. The homepage has fewer links competing for attention, and no longer contacts the exchange-rate service.',
    details: [
      'Topic pages (/blog/tag/...): a topic\'s lessons are grouped by level on the same cards as the level pages, each group linking to its full level. The search box, the level summary and the topic chips are gone. Searching across every lesson happens on /blog/, which keeps what you type on the page. Before, the topic-page search wrote it into the address (?q=), which the analytics script then removed before sending any event; now nothing writes it there at all. The analytics script still strips ?q= from learning path addresses, for old bookmarks and hand-typed links.',
