      'Homepage: one main button per screen. Each of the four starting routes is now a single line that links to its route, instead of a card with a link per lesson, a link per free tool and a button; the line keeps the button\'s label (home-start-basics-door, home-start-no-plan-door, home-start-habits-door, home-start-complex-door) and still leads to the first lesson on the route you have not read, from the existing nidhi-reading-progress key. The hero no longer has the "Not sure where to begin?" and "Already know the basics?" lines. Labels removed with them: home-hero-first-lesson, home-hero-skip-building, home-hero-skip-psychology, home-hero-skip-tools, the per-lesson route links home-start-<route>-1, -2 and -3, and the per-tool route links home-start-<route>-tool-<n>. The Inclusive Finances route is a single line too, with its existing label (home-inclusive-finances). The "Welcome back" link (home-hero-continue) now shows only to readers with reading progress, as before. Nothing new is stored or sent.',
      'Homepage: the page is arranged as three steps (learn, see yours, look ahead). The worked example is split across them, with a short summary of it in the hero; the "nidhi grows with your financial life" section is removed, and the free tools are listed on their own, without a lesson link beside each one. Labels removed: home-grows-<stage>-1 and -2 for each stage, home-start-complex-more, home-pair-lesson-<tool> for each tool, and home-tools-all. Nothing new is stored or sent.',
      'Homepage: the multi-currency example and its "Add it up in euros at today\'s rates" button are removed, so the homepage no longer contacts Frankfurter (the European Central Bank exchange-rate service) at all. Its labels go with it: home-mc-convert and home-mc-tool. The net worth calculator still fetches rates as before, and the section on Frankfurter above no longer mentions the homepage.',
